# Local-only leak denylist for the pre-commit scan (.githooks/leak-scan.sh).
#
# Copy this file to ".leak-denylist.local" (which is gitignored) and fill in the
# REAL private terms that must never be committed to this PUBLIC repo. The real
# values live only in that local copy, so they never themselves leak here.
#
# Format: one POSIX extended-regex per line. Blank lines and '#' comments are
# ignored. Matching is case-insensitive. Use \b...\b for short common words to
# avoid false positives on substrings.
#
# Categories worth covering (replace the placeholders with your actual values):
#
#   # personal names (family, kids, etc.)
#   \bplaceholdername\b
#
#   # the private infrastructure repo this integration is developed alongside
#   your-private-repo-name
#
#   # internal hostnames / private domains
#   internal-host-name
#   private\.example\.com
#
#   # unrelated private projects that shouldn't be referenced here
#   SomeOtherPrivateProject
#
#   # private paths / secret-tooling identifiers
#   /var/lib/your-namespace
